{"parent_urn": "urn:li:activity:7437098653531516928", "parent_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7437098653531516928/", "parent_author_name": null, "parent_author_handle": "ross-nicholson-742072158", "is_reply_to_comment": true, "comment_text": "Ross Nicholson yes Ross this is 100% true. It\u2019s almost moving at supersonic speeds now every three months huge upgrades and updates. I\u2019d say the best is to learn how to apply it to your day-to-day activities and workflows this way it gives you time to elevate yourself to focus your brain power on the problems that matter strategy, higher level, decision making, etc.", "posted_label": "2mo"}
{"parent_urn": "urn:li:activity:7436054215191527424", "parent_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7436054215191527424/", "parent_author_name": null, "parent_author_handle": "faroukhajjej", "is_reply_to_comment": true, "comment_text": "Farouk Hajjej I will be straight up here I have only been playing with openclaw for about a week extensively\u2026 it\u2019s not the be all do all for all tasks just some tasks\u2026 for keeping track I would say: logs\u2026 the best way to monitor is through just telling it to log everything it does.. you can specify the level of detail you want\u2026 you could have a skill that does this for you periodically just watch out the tokens\u2026 I would test it runnng first perhaps you could make it so that it creates an independent log every 3 hours\u2026 this way it is easier to reference rather than having to deal with one huge file with 24 hours of logging\u2026 your openclaw should already be logging stuff just might not be exactly what you want to keep track of which are the tasks that it is supposed to be running in the heartbeat file or the cron jobs\u2026 lastly today something came to mind about this specific point what it you want to build an authentication tool or skill that checks every critical task against your criteria of tasks allowed to run and use your passwords and logins for specific tasks and actions\u2026 i am sure openai and preplexity computer etc these guys must have built some sort of internal tool for it\u2026 although recently preplexitys had a fall out!", "posted_label": "2mo"}
